. * ---- Treatment timing -----------------------------------------------------
> ----------
. * post = 1 from 2021H2 (DL 77/2021 from 1 Jun 2021). WHY a SINGLE interaction
> ?
. * With authority and half-year FE, exposure×pre and exposure×post are colline
> ar
. * with the authority FE; only their difference is identified. The existing
. * script estimated both and got 0.0000 (0.0000). Here only exposure×post ente
> rs.
. gen byte post = (halfyear >= yh(2021,2))
. gen byte p1 = inlist(halfyear, yh(2020,2), yh(2021,1))
. if "$NET_PRE" == "P0" gen byte main6 = inrange(halfyear, yh(2018,1), yh(2023,
> 1)) & p1 == 0
. * P1b mirror: pre = 2021H1 only (the one half-year entirely in P1b; 2020H2 mi
> xes
. * P1a, when services/supplies could be awarded directly up to the EU threshol
> d)
. else gen byte main6 = inrange(halfyear, yh(2021,1), yh(2023,1))
. gen float exp_post = exposure * post
. label var exp_post "Exposure x Post"
. 
. * ---- Flexible control for the contract count (fallback for net_sparsity) --
> ------
. * WHY? With few contracts per half-year, an authority mechanically has few
. * suppliers and a high turnover, so rewire/exclusivity depend on the count. W
> e
. * absorb count bins (1..10 one by one, then 11–15, 16–20, 21–30, 31–50, 51–10
> 0,
. * >100). CAVEAT: the count may itself respond to the reform (bad control), so
. * results are shown with and without it, and log count is reported as an outc
> ome.
. gen int ncbin = net_n_contracts if net_n_contracts <= 10
